Description: native Qt 6 reader for e-Sword modules
 eSword4Linux reads e-Sword Bible, commentary, dictionary, lexicon, topic,
 devotional, harmony, map and reference modules from a folder selected by the
 user. Files are opened read-only and are never modified.
 .
 The application uses a private Python and Qt runtime under /opt/esword4linux
 while relying on the distribution's /usr/bin/python3 interpreter. It supports
 X11 and Wayland sessions through Qt's xcb and Wayland platform plugins and
 keeps settings and search indexes in the XDG user directories.
 .
 No e-Sword modules are included; users must supply their own module folder.
